>// Since Signal Definition is a proxy resource, we cannot use Azure Tags [](http://example.com/codeflow?start=51&length=72)

I thought you CAN use tags.
@rkmanda is that right?

The code slices method up to the first dot without checking if a dot exists; if strings.Index returns -1, this will produce an unintended substring. Add a check for index < 0 and return an error before slicing.
```suggestion
	dotIndex := strings.Index(method, ".")
	if dotIndex < 0 {
		return nil, nonRetriableError{errors.New("invalid method format: missing '.' in method string")}
	}
	client := method[:dotIndex]
```
